														Thanks for posting info here guys.  Am working on fleshing out a few more ideas for RaidNight.  A few I've discussed in earlier forums, but lets see what gets posted:<br />
<br />
Ideas: <br />
<br />
1.) Setting up 3 RaidNights.  One leader for each one.  Each leader will be responsible for a chunk of our membership ie: 15-23, 24-30, 30+.  Among those tiers there will be a weekly raid for like level toons.  Maybe once a month we can bring all three squads together for a zone that can be done at all levels.  I was hoping maybe Sanadeb would take a day, and possibly Garlin or Sittingbull taking a day.  Post more here..<br />
<br />
2.)  Setting up base suits of equipment for our newbie alts and new members.  I'm not talking stellar stuff here.  I'm just thinking at least a full suit of avg-good crafted armor.  A few low level jewelcrafted rings (+2,+3) and a decent weapon.  Please feel free to email me more regarding this idea.  I can Tailor like a madman, but do we have any jewelers out there that can make cheap rings/earrings.  Plus we can hoard up some Fine Steel weapons.  Or even find a nice weapon/class combo that we can consistently pick up somewheres.   I think it'd be nice to be able to invite someone in and then proceed to flush out there equipment list.  We then can appoint someone as quartermaster for our newbies/ or have a &quot;mentor&quot; for each class that would outfit the respective newbies.  Just shooting from the hip here, whaddya think.<br />
<br />
3.)  Sister Guild organizations.  I have a few friends from other guilds in RL.  I was wondering if a Sister guild might be an intriguing concept for any of y'all.  Since they have a few more higher ups than we do, they'd be able to take a few of us on planar raids as a learning experiment?  Plus who knows maybe we'd be able to set up a few guildwars, get a little rivaly set up between guilds.  I know that the Roleplay aspect of meeting your archnemesis would be a real treat.  Plus we could set a one day war (with plenty of advance notice) maybe once a month.  Who knows<br />
<br />
